    "key_findings": [
      "1. Regime-switching does NOT solve the BTC 1%/5% VaR mutual exclusion",
      "2. All 4 regime methods (RV, VIX, GMM, Adaptive) pass 1% but fail 5% — identical to Normal",
      "3. Root cause: 2023-2024 is 87-92% low-vol regime, so regime switching degenerates to pure Normal",
      "4. RV-Regime: only 59/731 days (8.1%) classified as high-vol — too few for Student-t to affect 5% coverage",
      "5. VIX-Regime: only 101/731 days (13.8%) with VIX>=20 — still insufficient",
      "6. Adaptive-Blend: mean weight=0.137 (87% Normal), only 2.9% of days near-Student-t",
      "7. At 5% VaR: regime methods get 22-24 violations (need ~37 to pass Kupiec), Student-t gets 33",
      "8. The problem is GARCH variance over-prediction during bull runs, not distributional misspecification",
      "9. DM test: VIX-Regime significantly better than Normal at 5% pinball (DM=-3.49, p<0.001) but still fails Trinity",
      "10. Fundamental impossibility: when GARCH sigma is too high, both Normal and Student-t VaR are too conservative — switching between them cannot fix the sigma"
    ],
    "practical_implication": "Simple regime-switching between Normal and Student-t quantiles cannot solve the BTC VaR mutual exclusion. The 1%/5% split is caused by GARCH variance over-prediction during prolonged bull runs (mean return 0.27%/day in 2023-2024). The fix must come from the variance model (e.g., lower persistence, variance targeting, or regime-switching GARCH with separate parameter sets per regime) rather than from the distribution. For practitioners: use Normal at 1% and Student-t at 5% as separate models.",
    "limitations": [
      "OOS 2023-2024 is a bull market period; bear market results may differ dramatically",
      "BTC trades 24/7 but VIX only weekdays — forward-fill introduces lag",
      "Simple regime detection; full Hamilton filter or MS-GARCH (with separate GARCH params per regime) may perform differently",
      "Only GJR-GARCH variance model tested; EGARCH, HAR-RV, or realized measures could change results",
      "Regime threshold sensitivity not fully explored (e.g., lower RV percentile could increase Student-t usage)"
    ]
  }
